    "created_at": "2020-10-01T16:13:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-10-01T16:32:56Z",
    "body": "I have just installed the most recent version 0.45.2 via Homebrew on macOS 10.15.7 with fish 3.1.2 and notice my custom symbol is being ignored. Never had this happen before with starship.\r\n\r\n```\r\n# ~/.config/starship.toml\r\n\r\n[character]\r\nsymbol = \"#\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nCan I do anything to help troubleshoot this issue?\r\n\r\nDowngrading to version 0.44.0 does resolve this issue, so it appears there might be a regression. To work around this issue for the time being, here are the steps I took to downgrade (fish shell):\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd (brew --repo homebrew/core)\r\ngit checkout -b starship-0.44.0_1 faad9048c1a533df04af280a9135049dfcf924d0\r\nbrew unlink starship\r\nenv HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1 brew install starship\r\nbrew pin starship\r\ngit checkout master\r\ngit branch -d starship-0.44.0_1\r\nbrew cleanup\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
